tool_calls.arguments:
{"command":"cat <<EOF > nginx-custom-default.conf
user nginx;
worker_processes auto;
error_log /var/log/nginx/error.log;
pid /var/run/nginx.pid;

events {
    worker_connections 1024;
}

http {
    include mime.types;
    default_type application/octet-stream;

    # Redirect temporary file handling to the writable volume
    client_temp_path /usr/share/nginx/html/writable/temp;

    log_format main '$remote_addr - $remote_user [$time_local] "$request" '
                       '$status $body_bytes_sent "$http_referer" '
                       '"$http_user_agent"';

    server {
        listen 80 default_server;
        server_name localhost;
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html;
    }
}
EOF
kubectl create configmap nginx-custom-default --from-file=default.conf=nginx-custom-default.conf"}

messages.reasoning_content:
The `kubectl rollout status` command timed out (error: context deadline exceeded). This confirms the rollout is stalled, meaning the new pod is not reaching a stable ready state, which is consistent with the `CrashLoopBackOff` observed previously, even if logs are now empty.

Since the primary suspect (`client_temp_path`) has been addressed by injecting a writable volume and config, and the failure persists, the next smallest change is to remove the custom configuration file mount and rely solely on the writable volume patch, in case the configuration injection introduced a new failure mode.

If Nginx can use the writable volume without explicit configuration change, that is the smallest change that addresses the original problem while keeping RORFS.

I will revert the configuration patch, keeping only the writable volume patch.

First, revert the ConfigMap patch:
The previous patch was:
```yaml
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "volumeMounts": [
              {
                "name": "writable-data",
                "mountPath": "/usr/share/nginx/html/writable"
              },
              {
                "name": "nginx-config-volume",
                "mountPath": "/etc/nginx/nginx.conf",
                "subPath": ""
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "volumes": [
          {
            "name": "writable-data",
            "emptyDir": {}
          },
          {
            "name": "nginx-config-volume",
            "configMap": {
              "name": "nginx-custom-default"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
I need to patch to remove `nginx-config-volume` from `volumeMounts` and `volumes`.

Then, I must delete the ConfigMap `nginx-custom-default`.

This is the minimal justified change to revert the complexity and return to the simplest fix for the RORFS issue: providing a writable location.

